/*  A file checked where it sits — `BookLoading.Neighbours`, `ProjectTree` and `SourceMap` in C#.

    ★ A file inside a PROJECT — under a folder holding `blueprint.cufe` — is part of more than
    itself: the files of its folder, and of each folder above it in its namespace, are part of its
    program. Their declarations are brought in ahead of its own, and a name two of them declare is
    refused. A file under no project gets nothing, exactly as before.

    ★ Every loaded file is read at a line offset — 100,000 lines a file — so the whole program keeps
    one numbering and a refusal's position says which file it is in. A message is turned back into
    the file's own lines on the way out, as C#'s reporter does.

    ★ A folder of the namespace off the file's chain, or another namespace, is reached by qualifying
    it — `parser's program-tree` — and loaded only then, its names renamed `<name> in <where>` so a
    sibling may repeat any of them.

    ★ A book pulled from a file is loaded beside the file that pulls it, or from the project's
    `books/`, its own names hidden but its modules.

    ⚠ Paths are kept with `/` between their parts whatever the platform gives back.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    /// Where a line of the checked program came from: the file a block of lines belongs to.
    Define object source-block with (the number first-line, the text from-file).

    // ── Paths ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    Bind text to slashed, given (the text raw):
        Return replace "\\" with "/" in raw.
    Done.

    /// The folder a path is in, or "" at the top.
    Bind text to parent-of, given (the text full):
        Define letters as a chase.
        Insert full into letters.
        Define back as the number of letters.
        While back is greater than 0, repeat:
            If item back of letters is "/":
                If back is 1, return "/".
                Return the characters from 1 to (back - 1) of full.
            Done.
            Decrement back by 1.
        Done.
        Return "".
    Done.

    /// The last part of a path.
    Bind text to file-part, given (the text full):
        Define parent as cast parent-of on (full).
        If parent is "", return full.
        Return the characters from (the length of parent + 2) to the end of full.
    Done.

    /// A path made absolute against the current directory, its parts joined with `/`.
    Bind text to full-path, given (the text given-path):
        Define written as cast slashed on (given-path).
        If written starts with "/", return written.
        If the length of written is greater than 1 and (the characters from 2 to 2 of written) is ":", return written.
        Define here as cast slashed on (the current directory but void is "").
        If here ends with "/", return here joined to written.
        Return "{here}/{written}".
    Done.

    Bind fact to same-path, given (the text left, the text right):
        Return (left in lowercase) is (right in lowercase).
    Done.

    /// The nearest folder at or above this one holding a blueprint, or "".
    Bind text to project-root, given (the text folder):
        Define at as folder.
        While at is not "", repeat:
            If the path "{at}/blueprint.cufe" is a file, return at.
            Define up as cast parent-of on (at).
            If up is at, return "".
            The at becomes up.
        Done.
        Return "".
    Done.

    /// Every `.cufe` in a folder, sorted, or none when it cannot be read.
    Bind series of text to cufet-files, given (the text folder):
        Define found as a series of text.
        Try to:
            For each entry in the contents of the directory folder, repeat:
                Define entry-path as cast slashed on (entry).
                If entry-path ends with ".cufe" and the path entry-path is a file, insert entry-path into found.
            Done.
        Done.
        In case of failure:
            Return found.
        Done.
        Return found.
    Done.

    Bind series of text to sub-folders, given (the text folder):
        Define found as a series of text.
        Try to:
            For each entry in the contents of the directory folder, repeat:
                Define entry-path as cast slashed on (entry).
                If the path entry-path is a directory, insert entry-path into found.
            Done.
        Done.
        In case of failure:
            Return found.
        Done.
        Return found.
    Done.

    // ── Reading a loaded file ─────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// A copy of a tree that shares nothing a note could change — every node but its leaves is new.
    Bind node to copied-node, given (the node tree):
        If tree's kind is "atom", return tree.
        Define copy as a new node { the kind tree's kind, the word tree's word, the children a series of node }.
        For each child in tree's children, repeat:
            Insert cast copied-node on (child) into copy's children.
        Done.
        Return copy.
    Done.

    /// A file's statements, read at `offset` — parsed once per run for each offset, and handed out
    /// as a fresh copy every time, since checking writes notes into the tree it is given.
    Bind node or failure to loaded-tree unto checker, given (the text from-file, the text file-text, the number offset):
        Define key as "{offset}|{from-file}".
        Define cached as the entry for key in one's parse-cache.
        If cached is not void, return cast copied-node on (cached).
        Define parsed as cast parser's program-tree-from on (file-text, offset) or pass the failure off.
        In one's parse-cache, the entry for key becomes parsed.
        Return cast copied-node on (parsed).
    Done.

    // ── The source map ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// A new block of lines for a file — C#'s `SourceMap.Add`.
    Bind number to add-source unto checker, given (the text from-file):
        Define first as 100000 * (the number of one's source-blocks + 1).
        Insert a new source-block { the first-line first, the from-file from-file } into one's source-blocks.
        Return first.
    Done.

    /// A message with every line number from a loaded file turned back into that file's own —
    /// `SourceMap.Rewrite`: only a run of six digits or more, and only inside a block.
    Bind text to source-rewritten unto checker, given (the text message):
        If the number of one's source-blocks is 0, return message.
        Define letters as a chase.
        Insert message into letters.
        Define out as a chase.
        Define place as 1.
        Define count as the number of letters.
        While place is not greater than count, repeat:
            Define ch as item place of letters.
            If "0123456789" contains ch:
                Define digits as "".
                While place is not greater than count and "0123456789" contains (item place of letters), repeat:
                    The digits becomes digits joined to (item place of letters).
                    Increment place by 1.
                Done.
                Define shown as digits.
                If the length of digits is greater than 5:
                    Define value as (digits converted to number but void is 0).
                    For each block in one's source-blocks, repeat:
                        If value is not less than block's first-line and value is less than block's first-line + 100000:
                            The shown becomes (value - block's first-line) converted to text.
                        Done.
                    Done.
                Done.
                Insert shown into out.
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                Insert ch into out.
                Increment place by 1.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return out converted to text.
    Done.

    // ── The tree a blueprint draws (`ProjectTree`) ────────────────────────

    /// Every folder the drawing names, mapped to the folder whose namespace it is part of — or an
    /// empty map when the blueprint draws no tree.
    Bind map from text to text or failure to project-tree unto checker, given (the text root):
        Define drawn-in as a map from text to text.
        Define blueprint-path as "{root}/blueprint.cufe".
        Define file-text as "".
        Try to:
            The file-text becomes read all from the file blueprint-path.
        Done.
        In case of failure:
            Return drawn-in.
        Done.
        If (file-text in lowercase) contains "tree" is false, return drawn-in.
        Define offset as cast one's add-source on (blueprint-path).
        Define blueprint as cast one's loaded-tree on (blueprint-path, file-text, offset) or pass the failure off.
        Define tree-bind as cast unknown-type.
        For each statement in cast hoistable-in-pulls on (blueprint), repeat:
            If cast is-none on (tree-bind) and statement's kind is "BindStatement":
                If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)) and cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) is "tree":
                    The tree-bind becomes statement.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        If cast is-none on (tree-bind), return drawn-in.
        Define body as (cast field-of on (tree-bind, 4))'s children.
        Define written-out as (cast field-of on (tree-bind, 2))'s kind is "TextType" and the number of body is 1.
        If written-out:
            The written-out becomes (item 1 of body)'s kind is "ReturnStatement".
            If written-out, the written-out becomes (cast field-of on (item 1 of body, 1))'s kind is "StringLiteral".
        Done.
        If written-out is false:
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("the blueprint's 'tree' has to be written out, not worked out",
                "The tools read the tree without running anything, so its body can only give back the drawing itself",
                cast numeric on (cast field-of on (tree-bind, 7)), "work out the tree",
                "Write it as 'Bind text to tree:', then 'Return <<', a line for each folder, and '>>.'.")).
        Done.
        Define returned as item 1 of body.
        // Where the drawing starts: the `<<` after the `Return`, counted in the blueprint's own lines.
        Define lines as (replace "\r\n" with "\n" in file-text) split by "\n".
        Define return-line as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (returned, 2)) - offset.
        Define open-line as return-line.
        Define index as return-line.
        Define looking as true.
        While looking and index is not greater than the number of lines, repeat:
            If item index of lines contains "<<":
                The open-line becomes index.
                The looking becomes false.
            Done.
            Increment index by 1.
        Done.
        Define drawing as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (cast field-of on (returned, 1), 1)).
        Cast one's draw-tree on (drawing, root, offset + open-line, drawn-in) or pass the failure off.
        Cast require-every-source-folder on (root, offset + open-line, drawn-in) or pass the failure off.
        Return drawn-in.
    Done.

    /// Top-level statements, and those inside a `Pull` — where a blueprint's functions sit.
    Bind series of node to hoistable-in-pulls, given (the node statements):
        Define found as a series of node.
        For each statement in statements's children, repeat:
            Insert statement into found.
            If statement's kind is "PullStatement":
                For each inner in cast hoistable-in-pulls on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)), repeat:
                    Insert inner into found.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return found.
    Done.

    /// A folder as the drawing would name it, relative to the project root.
    Bind text to shown-folder, given (the text root, the text folder):
        If (folder in lowercase) starts with ((root in lowercase) joined to "/"):
            Return the characters from (the length of root + 2) to the end of folder.
        Done.
        Return folder.
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to draw-tree unto checker, given (the text drawing, the text root, the number first-line,
            the map from text to text drawn-in):
        Define drawn-at as a map from text to number.
        Define level-widths as a series of number.
        Define level-folders as a series of text.
        Define level-owners as a series of text.
        Define indent-with as "".
        Define lines as (replace "\r\n" with "\n" in drawing) split by "\n".
        Define index as 0.
        For each raw in lines, repeat:
            Increment index by 1.
            Define name as raw trimmed.
            If name is "", skip.
            Define at-line as first-line + index - 1.
            Define width as 0.
            Define letters as a chase.
            Insert raw into letters.
            While width is less than the number of letters and (item (width + 1) of letters is " " or item (width + 1) of letters is "\t"), repeat:
                Define ch as item (width + 1) of letters.
                If indent-with is "", the indent-with becomes ch.
                If ch is not indent-with:
                    Define with-what as "spaces".
                    If ch is "\t", the with-what becomes "a tab".
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("the tree's drawing mixes tabs and spaces", "",
                        at-line, "indent '{name}' with {with-what}",
                        "Indent the whole drawing one way — all spaces or all tabs — so a folder's depth means one thing.")).
                Done.
                Increment width by 1.
            Done.
            Define folder as "".
            Define owner as "".
            If width is 0:
                While the number of level-widths is greater than 0, repeat:
                    Remove item (the number of level-widths) from level-widths.
                    Remove item (the number of level-folders) from level-folders.
                    Remove item (the number of level-owners) from level-owners.
                Done.
                The folder becomes "{root}/{name}".
                The owner becomes folder.
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                Define dedented as false.
                While the number of level-widths is greater than 0 and item (the number of level-widths) of level-widths is greater than width, repeat:
                    Remove item (the number of level-widths) from level-widths.
                    Remove item (the number of level-folders) from level-folders.
                    Remove item (the number of level-owners) from level-owners.
                    The dedented becomes true.
                Done.
                Define same-level as false.
                If the number of level-widths is greater than 0, the same-level becomes item (the number of level-widths) of level-widths is width.
                If same-level:
                    Remove item (the number of level-widths) from level-widths.
                    Remove item (the number of level-folders) from level-folders.
                    Remove item (the number of level-owners) from level-owners.
                Done.
                Otherwise if dedented:
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' is indented to a depth no folder above it has", "",
                        at-line, "indent '{name}' between two levels",
                        "Line it up with the folder it sits beside, or indent it further than the folder it belongs to.")).
                Done.
                If the number of level-widths is 0:
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' is indented, but there is no folder above it to belong to", "",
                        at-line, "indent '{name}'",
                        "Start the drawing at the left edge — a folder there is a namespace of its own.")).
                Done.
                The folder becomes "{item (the number of level-folders) of level-folders}/{name}".
                The owner becomes item (the number of level-owners) of level-owners.
            Done.
            Define shown as cast shown-folder on (root, folder).
            If the path folder is a directory is false:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("the tree draws '{shown}', but there is no such folder", "",
                    at-line, "draw '{shown}'",
                    "Create the folder, or take its line out — the tree describes the folders the project has; it does not make them.")).
            Done.
            Define first-drawn as the entry for (folder in lowercase) in drawn-at.
            If first-drawn is not void:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("the tree draws '{shown}' twice", "It is first drawn on line {first-drawn}",
                    at-line, "draw '{shown}' again", "Take one of the two lines out.")).
            Done.
            In drawn-at, the entry for (folder in lowercase) becomes at-line.
            In drawn-in, the entry for folder becomes owner.
            Insert width into level-widths.
            Insert folder into level-folders.
            Insert owner into level-owners.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// Once a project draws its tree, it draws every folder with Cufet source in it.
    Bind void or failure to require-every-source-folder, given (the text root, the number at-line,
            the map from text to text drawn-in):
        Define drawn-names as a map from text to fact.
        For each pair in drawn-in, repeat:
            In drawn-names, the entry for (the key of pair in lowercase) becomes true.
        Done.
        Define found as a series of text.
        Cast walk-source-folders on (root, "{root}/books", true, found).
        For each folder in found, repeat:
            If (the entry for (folder in lowercase) in drawn-names) is void:
                Define shown as cast shown-folder on (root, folder).
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("the folder '{shown}' holds Cufet source, and the tree does not draw it",
                    "Once a project draws its tree it draws every folder, so the drawing can be trusted to be the whole project",
                    at-line, "leave '{shown}' out of the tree",
                    "Add a line for it — at the left edge for a namespace of its own, or indented under the folder it belongs to.")).
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// Whether a folder holds Cufet source in it or beneath it, adding each such folder below the
    /// root to `found` in path order.
    Bind fact to walk-source-folders, given (the text folder, the text books, the fact is-root, the series of text found):
        If cast same-path on (folder, books), return false.
        Define at as the number of found.
        Define any as the number of cast cufet-files on (folder) is greater than 0.
        Define below as a series of text.
        For each child in cast sub-folders on (folder), repeat:
            If cast walk-source-folders on (child, books, false, below), the any becomes true.
        Done.
        If any and is-root is false, insert folder into found.
        For each child in below, repeat:
            Insert child into found.
        Done.
        Return any.
    Done.

    /// The folder whose namespace this one's files belong to — itself unless the tree folds it.
    Bind text to namespace-of, given (the map from text to text drawn-in, the text folder):
        For each pair in drawn-in, repeat:
            If cast same-path on (the key of pair, folder), return the value of pair.
        Done.
        Return folder.
    Done.

    /// A folder and each above it, up to and including its namespace's folder.
    Bind series of text to folder-chain, given (the text folder, the text namespace-folder):
        Define chain as a series of text.
        Define at as folder.
        While at is not "", repeat:
            Insert at into chain.
            If cast same-path on (at, namespace-folder), return chain.
            Define up as cast parent-of on (at).
            If up is at, return chain.
            The at becomes up.
        Done.
        Return chain.
    Done.

    /// Every folder that is its own namespace — holding Cufet, or with a folder folded into it that
    /// does — keyed by the name that qualifies it (`BookLoading.Namespaces`).
    Bind void to gather-namespaces, given (the text folder, the text books, the map from text to text drawn-in,
            the map from text to series of text found):
        If cast same-path on (folder, books), return.
        Define own-source as false.
        For each one-file in cast cufet-files on (folder), repeat:
            If (cast file-part on (one-file) in lowercase) is not "blueprint.cufe", the own-source becomes true.
        Done.
        Define folded as cast namespace-of on (drawn-in, folder) is not folder.
        Define folded-source as false.
        For each pair in drawn-in, repeat:
            If cast same-path on (the value of pair, folder) and cast same-path on (the key of pair, folder) is false:
                If the number of cast cufet-files on (the key of pair) is greater than 0, the folded-source becomes true.
            Done.
        Done.
        If folded is false and (own-source or folded-source):
            Define key as cast file-part on (folder) in lowercase.
            If (the entry for key in found) is void, in found, the entry for key becomes a series of text.
            Define list as the entry for key in found but void is a series of text.
            Insert folder into list.
        Done.
        For each child in cast sub-folders on (folder), repeat:
            Cast gather-namespaces on (child, books, drawn-in, found).
        Done.
    Done.

    // ── What a folder contributes (`Gathered`) ────────────────────────────

    /// Every name a file's top level declares, as `[name line column]` — `TopLevelNames`.
    Bind series of node to top-level-names, given (the node statements):
        Define found as a series of node.
        For each statement in cast hoistable on (statements), repeat:
            Define kind as statement's kind.
            Define named as false.
            If kind is "ObjectDefinition" or kind is "InterfaceDefinition", the named becomes true.
            If kind is "BindStatement" and cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)), the named becomes true.
            If kind is "DefineStatement" and cast truth-of on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)), the named becomes true.
            If named:
                Define line-place as 5.
                If kind is "ObjectDefinition", the line-place becomes 9.
                If kind is "BindStatement", the line-place becomes 7.
                If kind is "InterfaceDefinition", the line-place becomes 3.
                Insert cast made on ("list", a series with (cast field-of on (statement, 1), cast field-of on (statement, line-place),
                    cast field-of on (statement, line-place + 1))) into found.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return found.
    Done.

    /// What a neighbour contributes: everything it declares, and nothing it does.
    Bind node to declarations-only, given (the node statements):
        Define kept as cast listed.
        For each statement in statements's children, repeat:
            Define kind as statement's kind.
            If kind is "PullStatement" or kind is "PullRabbitStatement":
                Cast kept's add on (cast with-field on (statement, 2, cast declarations-only on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)))).
            Done.
            Otherwise if kind is "DefineStatement":
                If cast truth-of on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)), cast kept's add on (statement).
            Done.
            Otherwise if kind is "BindStatement" or kind is "ObjectDefinition" or kind is "InterfaceDefinition"
                    or kind is "GetterDeclaration" or kind is "SetterDeclaration" or kind is "UnmakerDeclaration"
                    or kind is "OperatorOverloadDeclaration":
                Cast kept's add on (statement).
            Done.
        Done.
        Return kept.
    Done.

    /// The statements a folder contributes, its names claimed in `claimed` (lowercased name → file).
    Bind node or failure to gathered-from unto checker, given (the text folder, the text skip-file,
            the map from text to text claimed):
        Define gathered as cast listed.
        For each one-file in cast cufet-files on (folder), repeat:
            Define skipping as (cast file-part on (one-file) in lowercase) is "blueprint.cufe".
            If skip-file is not "" and cast same-path on (one-file, skip-file), the skipping becomes true.
            If skipping is false:
                Define file-text as "".
                Try to:
                    The file-text becomes read all from the file one-file.
                Done.
                In case of failure:
                    Define shown as cast file-part on (one-file).
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{shown}' is in this directory but could not be read",
                        the message of the failure, 0, "read '{shown}' as part of its directory", "Check the file's permissions.")).
                Done.
                Define offset as cast one's add-source on (one-file).
                Define inner as cast one's loaded-tree on (one-file, file-text, offset) or pass the failure off.
                For each named in cast top-level-names on (inner), repeat:
                    Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (named, 1)).
                    Define at-line as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (named, 2)).
                    Define key as name in lowercase.
                    Define already as the entry for key in claimed.
                    If already is void:
                        In claimed, the entry for key becomes one-file.
                    Done.
                    Otherwise:
                        If cast same-path on (cast parent-of on (already), cast parent-of on (one-file)) is false:
                            Return a failure (cast name-above on (name, cast parent-of on (already), cast parent-of on (one-file), at-line)).
                        Done.
                        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' is declared in two files of one directory",
                            "'{cast file-part on (already)}' declares it too, and a directory is one namespace — its files share a single set of names, with nothing between them to keep two apart",
                            at-line, "declare '{name}' in '{cast file-part on (one-file)}' as well",
                            "Rename one of them, or move one of the two files into a directory of its own — a directory is what separates one set of names from another.")).
                    Done.
                Done.
                For each kept in (cast declarations-only on (inner))'s children, repeat:
                    Cast gathered's add on (kept).
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return gathered.
    Done.

    /// The refusal for a folder declaring a name a folder above it already has.
    Bind text to name-above, given (the text name, the text folder, the text up, the number at-line):
        Define here as cast file-part on (folder).
        Define above as cast file-part on (up).
        Return cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' is declared in '{here}' and in '{above}' above it",
            "A folder sees every name the folders above it declare, so '{here}' would have two meanings for it, and the nearer would win without a word",
            at-line, "declare '{name}' in '{here}' as well",
            "Rename one of them. Folders beside each other may share a name; a folder and one above it may not.").
    Done.

    // ── Neighbours ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// The program with what its folder and the folders above it declare brought in ahead of it, and
    /// every folder or namespace it qualifies loaded under its own names — unchanged when the file is
    /// in no project.
    Bind node or failure to with-neighbours unto checker, given (the node statements):
        If one's source-file is "", return statements.
        Define self as one's source-file.
        If (cast file-part on (self) in lowercase) is "blueprint.cufe", return statements.
        Define folder as cast parent-of on (self).
        Define root as cast project-root on (folder).
        If root is "", return statements.
        Define drawn-in as cast one's project-tree on (root) or pass the failure off.
        Define namespace-folder as cast namespace-of on (drawn-in, folder).

        // ── Its own folder, and each folder above it in its namespace ────────
        Define own-chain as cast folder-chain on (folder, namespace-folder).
        Define claimed as a map from text to text.
        For each named in cast top-level-names on (statements), repeat:
            In claimed, the entry for (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (named, 1)) in lowercase) becomes self.
        Done.
        Define here as cast listed.
        For each chain-folder in own-chain, repeat:
            For each brought in (cast one's gathered-from on (chain-folder, self, claimed) or pass the failure off)'s children, repeat:
                Cast here's add on (brought).
            Done.
        Done.

        // ── What it qualifies, loaded on demand, to a fixpoint ───────────────
        Define every-namespace as a map from text to series of text.
        Cast gather-namespaces on (root, "{root}/books", drawn-in, every-namespace).
        Define own-name as cast file-part on (namespace-folder).
        Define chain-names as a map from text to fact.
        For each chain-folder in own-chain, repeat:
            In chain-names, the entry for (cast file-part on (chain-folder) in lowercase) becomes true.
        Done.
        Define folders as cast other-folders on (drawn-in, namespace-folder, own-chain).

        // A qualifier's members: lowercased qualifier → lowercased member → the name it now has.
        Define reach as a map from text to map from text to text.
        // Another namespace loaded, by the qualifier as written: its statements.
        Define loaded as a map from text to node.
        Define loaded-order as a series of text.
        // A folder of this namespace loaded under its own rename, by path.
        Define renamed-statements as a map from text to node.
        Define renamed-names as a map from text to map from text to text.
        Define renamed-order as a series of text.

        Define frontier as a series of node with (statements, here).
        While the number of frontier is greater than 0, repeat:
            Define wanted as a map from text to node.
            Define wanted-order as a series of text.
            For each group in frontier, repeat:
                Define found as a series of node.
                Cast gather-qualifier-sites on (group, found).
                For each site in found, repeat:
                    Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (site, 1)).
                    Define key as name in lowercase.
                    If (the entry for key in reach) is void and (the entry for key in chain-names) is void
                            and ((the entry for key in every-namespace) is not void or (the entry for key in folders) is not void)
                            and (the entry for name in wanted) is void:
                        In wanted, the entry for name becomes site.
                        Insert name into wanted-order.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
            The frontier becomes a series of node.
            For each name in cast sorted-texts on (wanted-order), repeat:
                Define site as the entry for name in wanted but void is cast nothing.
                Define key as name in lowercase.
                Define directories as a series of text.
                Define in-namespaces as the entry for key in every-namespace but void is a series of text.
                Define in-here as the entry for key in folders but void is a series of text.
                For each one-folder in in-namespaces, repeat:
                    Insert one-folder into directories.
                Done.
                For each one-folder in in-here, repeat:
                    Insert one-folder into directories.
                Done.
                If the number of directories is greater than 1:
                    Define listing as "".
                    For each one-folder in directories, repeat:
                        If listing is not "", the listing becomes listing joined to " and ".
                        The listing becomes listing joined to "'{cast native-path on (one-folder)}'".
                    Done.
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("two directories of this project are both named '{name}'",
                        "They are {listing}, and a directory is reached by its name — so this qualification would have two meanings",
                        cast numeric on (cast field-of on (site, 2)), "qualify with '{name}'",
                        "Rename one of them. A qualifier reaches one directory, and which one has to be decidable from the name alone.")).
                Done.
                If the number of in-here is greater than 0:
                    // A folder of this namespace: it, and each folder above it off this file's chain.
                    For each up-folder in cast folder-chain on (item 1 of in-here, namespace-folder), repeat:
                        Define on-chain as false.
                        For each chain-folder in own-chain, repeat:
                            If cast same-path on (chain-folder, up-folder), the on-chain becomes true.
                        Done.
                        If on-chain, stop.
                        If (the entry for up-folder in renamed-statements) is void:
                            Define gathered as cast one's gathered-from on (up-folder, "", a map from text to text) or pass the failure off.
                            Define names as a map from text to text.
                            For each named in cast top-level-names on (gathered), repeat:
                                Define member as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (named, 1)).
                                In names, the entry for (member in lowercase) becomes "{member} in {cast shown-folder on (root, up-folder)}".
                            Done.
                            In renamed-statements, the entry for up-folder becomes gathered.
                            In renamed-names, the entry for up-folder becomes names.
                            Insert up-folder into renamed-order.
                            Insert gathered into frontier.
                        Done.
                    Done.
                    In reach, the entry for key becomes the entry for (item 1 of in-here) in renamed-names but void is a map from text to text.
                Done.
                Otherwise:
                    // Another namespace: reached by its own folder's names.
                    Define other as cast one's gathered-from on (item 1 of directories, "", a map from text to text) or pass the failure off.
                    In loaded, the entry for name becomes other.
                    Insert name into loaded-order.
                    Define members as a map from text to text.
                    For each named in cast top-level-names on (other), repeat:
                        Define member as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (named, 1)).
                        In members, the entry for (member in lowercase) becomes "{member} in {name}".
                    Done.
                    In reach, the entry for key becomes members.
                    Insert other into frontier.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.

        // A name a renamed folder declares that a folder above it declares too.
        For each renamed-folder in renamed-order, repeat:
            Define gathered as the entry for renamed-folder in renamed-statements but void is cast listed.
            For each named in cast top-level-names on (gathered), repeat:
                Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (named, 1)).
                Define key as name in lowercase.
                Define first-up as true.
                For each up-folder in cast folder-chain on (renamed-folder, namespace-folder), repeat:
                    If first-up:
                        The first-up becomes false.
                    Done.
                    Otherwise:
                        Define above as false.
                        Define upper as the entry for up-folder in renamed-names.
                        If upper is not void:
                            The above becomes (the entry for key in upper) is not void.
                        Done.
                        Otherwise:
                            Define claimer as the entry for key in claimed.
                            If claimer is not void, the above becomes cast same-path on (cast parent-of on (claimer), up-folder).
                        Done.
                        If above:
                            Return a failure (cast name-above on (name, renamed-folder, up-folder, cast numeric on (cast field-of on (named, 2)))).
                        Done.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.

        If the size of reach is 0:
            If the number of here's children is 0, return statements.
            For each statement in statements's children, repeat:
                Cast here's add on (statement).
            Done.
            Return here.
        Done.

        // ── The renames, and the qualifications that now point at them ───────
        Define qualifiers as a map from text to fact.
        For each pair in every-namespace, repeat:
            In qualifiers, the entry for the key of pair becomes true.
        Done.
        For each pair in folders, repeat:
            In qualifiers, the entry for the key of pair becomes true.
        Done.
        // What was written is left as it was — a copy is qualified, so the program held whole is not.
        Define written as cast copied-node on (statements).
        For each name in loaded-order, repeat:
            Define group as the entry for name in loaded but void is cast listed.
            Cast refuse-a-shadowed-namespace on (group, qualifiers, name) or pass the failure off.
            Cast refuse-a-member-not-there on (group, reach) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        For each renamed-folder in renamed-order, repeat:
            Define group as the entry for renamed-folder in renamed-statements but void is cast listed.
            Cast refuse-a-shadowed-namespace on (group, qualifiers, cast file-part on (renamed-folder)) or pass the failure off.
            Cast refuse-a-member-not-there on (group, reach) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Cast refuse-a-shadowed-namespace on (here, qualifiers, own-name) or pass the failure off.
        Cast refuse-a-member-not-there on (here, reach) or pass the failure off.
        Cast refuse-a-shadowed-namespace on (written, qualifiers, own-name) or pass the failure off.
        Cast refuse-a-member-not-there on (written, reach) or pass the failure off.

        Define brought as cast listed.
        For each name in cast sorted-texts on (loaded-order), repeat:
            Define group as the entry for name in loaded but void is cast listed.
            Cast qualify on (group, reach).
            Cast make-private on (group, name, a map from text to text, false).
            For each statement in group's children, repeat:
                Cast brought's add on (statement).
            Done.
        Done.
        For each renamed-folder in cast sorted-texts on (renamed-order), repeat:
            Define group as the entry for renamed-folder in renamed-statements but void is cast listed.
            // Its references to renamed folders above it follow those renames.
            Define above-names as a map from text to text.
            Define first-up as true.
            For each up-folder in cast folder-chain on (renamed-folder, namespace-folder), repeat:
                If first-up:
                    The first-up becomes false.
                Done.
                Otherwise:
                    Define upper as the entry for up-folder in renamed-names.
                    If upper is not void:
                        For each pair in upper, repeat:
                            If (the entry for the key of pair in above-names) is void, in above-names, the entry for the key of pair becomes the value of pair.
                        Done.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
            Cast qualify on (group, reach).
            Cast make-private on (group, cast shown-folder on (root, renamed-folder), above-names, false).
            For each statement in group's children, repeat:
                Cast brought's add on (statement).
            Done.
        Done.
        Cast qualify on (here, reach).
        Cast qualify on (written, reach).
        For each statement in here's children, repeat:
            Cast brought's add on (statement).
        Done.
        For each statement in written's children, repeat:
            Cast brought's add on (statement).
        Done.
        Return brought.
    Done.

    /// Texts in ordinal order — C#'s `StringComparer.Ordinal`.
    Bind series of text to sorted-texts, given (the series of text unsorted):
        Return unsorted sorted.
    Done.

    /// A path as the platform writes it, for a message that shows one whole.
    Bind text to native-path, given (the text full):
        If (the characters from 2 to 2 of full) is ":", return replace "/" with "\\" in full.
        Return full.
    Done.

    /// The folders of a namespace off this file's chain, keyed by the lowercased name that qualifies them.
    Bind map from text to series of text to other-folders, given (the map from text to text drawn-in,
            the text namespace-folder, the series of text own-chain):
        Define found as a map from text to series of text.
        Define members as a series of text.
        For each pair in drawn-in, repeat:
            If cast same-path on (the value of pair, namespace-folder) and cast same-path on (the key of pair, namespace-folder) is false:
                Insert the key of pair into members.
            Done.
        Done.
        For each member-folder in cast sorted-texts on (members), repeat:
            Define on-chain as false.
            For each chain-folder in own-chain, repeat:
                If cast same-path on (chain-folder, member-folder), the on-chain becomes true.
            Done.
            If on-chain is false:
                Define key as cast file-part on (member-folder) in lowercase.
                If (the entry for key in found) is void, in found, the entry for key becomes a series of text.
                Define list as the entry for key in found but void is a series of text.
                Insert member-folder into list.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return found.
    Done.

    /// Every `X's y` with `X` a name, as `[X line column]`.
    Bind void to gather-qualifier-sites, given (the node tree, the series of node found):
        If tree's kind is "atom", return.
        If tree's kind is "PossessiveAccess" and (cast field-of on (tree, 1))'s kind is "VariableReference":
            Insert cast made on ("list", a series with (cast field-of on (cast field-of on (tree, 1), 1),
                cast field-of on (tree, 3), cast field-of on (tree, 4))) into found.
        Done.
        For each child in tree's children, repeat:
            Cast gather-qualifier-sites on (child, found).
        Done.
    Done.

    /// `terminals's read-key` becomes the one name that declaration now has — where it stands, and
    /// only where the namespace really declares the member.
    Bind void to qualify, given (the node tree, the map from text to map from text to text reach):
        If tree's kind is "atom", return.
        Define place as 0.
        For each child in tree's children, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Define lifted as "".
            If child's kind is "PossessiveAccess" and (cast field-of on (child, 1))'s kind is "VariableReference":
                Define members as the entry for (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (cast field-of on (child, 1), 1)) in lowercase) in reach.
                If members is not void:
                    The lifted becomes the entry for (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (child, 2)) in lowercase) in members but void is "".
                Done.
            Done.
            If lifted is "", cast qualify on (child, reach).
            Otherwise:
                Cast rewrite-field on (tree, place, cast made on ("VariableReference", a series with (cast quoted on (lifted),
                    cast field-of on (child, 3), cast field-of on (child, 4)))).
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// A declaration named after a directory of this project — refused, so a qualification has one reading.
    Bind void or failure to refuse-a-shadowed-namespace, given (the node statements, the map from text to fact qualifiers,
            the text group-name):
        For each statement in cast every-statement-in on (statements), repeat:
            Define kind as statement's kind.
            Define line-place as 0.
            If kind is "ObjectDefinition", the line-place becomes 9.
            If kind is "InterfaceDefinition", the line-place becomes 3.
            If kind is "DefineStatement", the line-place becomes 5.
            If kind is "BindStatement" and cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)), the line-place becomes 7.
            If line-place is not 0:
                Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
                If (name in lowercase) is not (group-name in lowercase) and (the entry for (name in lowercase) in qualifiers) is not void:
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' is a directory of this project, so it cannot also be a name",
                        "A directory is a namespace named after itself, and '{name}' is how anything outside it writes '{name}'s ‹something›' — so the two readings would be indistinguishable",
                        cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, line-place)), "declare '{name}'",
                        "Rename this one. The directory's name belongs to the directory.")).
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// `‹directory›'s ‹member›` where that directory declares no such thing.
    Bind void or failure to refuse-a-member-not-there, given (the node tree, the map from text to map from text to text reach):
        If tree's kind is "atom", return.
        If tree's kind is "PossessiveAccess" and (cast field-of on (tree, 1))'s kind is "VariableReference":
            Define target as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (cast field-of on (tree, 1), 1)).
            Define member as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (tree, 2)).
            Define members as the entry for (target in lowercase) in reach.
            If members is not void:
                If (the entry for (member in lowercase) in members) is void:
                    Define offered as a series of text.
                    For each pair in members, repeat:
                        Insert cast short-of on (the value of pair) into offered.
                    Done.
                    Define what as "'{target}' is a directory of this project and its files declare nothing".
                    If the number of offered is greater than 0:
                        The what becomes "What its files declare is {cast comma-joined on (cast sorted-texts on (offered))}".
                    Done.
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("the directory '{target}' declares nothing called '{member}'", what,
                        cast numeric on (cast field-of on (tree, 3)), "reach '{target}'s {member}'",
                        "Check the spelling, or declare it in one of that directory's files — everything a directory's files declare at their top level is what the directory offers.")).
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        For each child in tree's children, repeat:
            Cast refuse-a-member-not-there on (child, reach) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// The name before ` in ` — what the member was called where it was written.
    Bind text to short-of, given (the text lifted):
        Define at as the position of " in " in lifted but void is 0.
        If at is 0, return lifted.
        Return the characters from 1 to (at - 1) of lifted.
    Done.

    /// A group's own declarations renamed `<name> in <tag>`, and every reference to them — C#'s
    /// `MakePrivate`. A book's modules are its face and keep their names (`exempt-modules`); a
    /// directory offers everything alike. `also-renamed` names declared elsewhere whose references
    /// follow too.
    Bind void to make-private, given (the node statements, the text tag, the map from text to text also-renamed,
            the fact exempt-modules):
        Define hidden as a map from text to text.
        Define top as a map from text to fact.
        For each statement in statements's children, repeat:
            If statement's kind is "DefineStatement", in top, the entry for "{(cast field-of on (statement, 5))'s word}:{(cast field-of on (statement, 6))'s word}" becomes true.
        Done.
        For each statement in cast hoistable on (statements), repeat:
            Define kind as statement's kind.
            Define named as kind is "ObjectDefinition" or kind is "InterfaceDefinition".
            If kind is "ObjectDefinition" and exempt-modules:
                If cast conforms-as on (statement, "module") or cast conforms-as on (statement, "book") or cast conforms-as on (statement, "region"):
                    The named becomes false.
                Done.
            Done.
            If kind is "BindStatement" and cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)), the named becomes true.
            If kind is "DefineStatement":
                If cast truth-of on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)), the named becomes true.
                If (the entry for "{(cast field-of on (statement, 5))'s word}:{(cast field-of on (statement, 6))'s word}" in top) is not void, the named becomes true.
            Done.
            If named:
                Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
                In hidden, the entry for name becomes "{name} in {tag}".
            Done.
        Done.
        For each pair in also-renamed, repeat:
            If (the entry for the key of pair in hidden) is void, in hidden, the entry for the key of pair becomes the value of pair.
        Done.
        If the size of hidden is 0, return.
        Cast rename-references on (statements, hidden).
        For each statement in cast hoistable on (statements), repeat:
            Cast rename-declaration on (statement, hidden).
        Done.
    Done.

    /// Every type, name and literal naming a hidden declaration, renamed where it stands.
    Bind void to rename-references, given (the node tree, the map from text to text hidden):
        If tree's kind is "atom", return.
        If tree's kind is "VariableReference" or tree's kind is "ObjectLiteral":
            Define renamed-to as the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (tree, 1)) in hidden.
            If renamed-to is not void, cast rewrite-field on (tree, 1, cast quoted on (renamed-to)).
        Done.
        Define place as 0.
        For each child in tree's children, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Define renamed-type as false.
            If child's kind is "ObjectType":
                Define renamed-to as the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (child, 1)) in hidden.
                If renamed-to is not void:
                    Cast rewrite-field on (tree, place, cast made on ("ObjectType", a series with (cast quoted on (renamed-to), cast listed))).
                    The renamed-type becomes true.
                Done.
            Done.
            If renamed-type is false, cast rename-references on (child, hidden).
        Done.
    Done.

    /// The declaration itself renamed to match what now refers to it.
    Bind void to rename-declaration, given (the node statement, the map from text to text hidden):
        Define kind as statement's kind.
        If kind is "ObjectDefinition":
            Cast rename-field-text on (statement, 1, hidden).
            Cast rename-field-text on (statement, 7, hidden).
            For each conformed in (cast field-of on (statement, 8))'s children, repeat:
                Define renamed-to as the entry for cast unquoted on (conformed) in hidden.
                If renamed-to is not void:
                    Define place as 0.
                    Define index as 0.
                    For each other in (cast field-of on (statement, 8))'s children, repeat:
                        Increment index by 1.
                        If other's word is conformed's word, the place becomes index.
                    Done.
                    Cast rewrite-field on (cast field-of on (statement, 8), place, cast quoted on (renamed-to)).
                Done.
            Done.
            Return.
        Done.
        If kind is "BindStatement":
            Define target as cast field-of on (statement, 5).
            If cast is-nothing on (target) is false and (the entry for cast unquoted on (target) in hidden) is not void:
                Cast rename-field-text on (statement, 5, hidden).
                Return.
            Done.
            Define made-name as cast field-of on (statement, 6).
            If cast is-nothing on (made-name) is false and (the entry for cast unquoted on (made-name) in hidden) is not void:
                Cast rename-field-text on (statement, 1, hidden).
                Cast rename-field-text on (statement, 6, hidden).
                Return.
            Done.
            Cast rename-field-text on (statement, 1, hidden).
            Return.
        Done.
        If kind is "GetterDeclaration":
            Cast rename-field-text on (statement, 4, hidden).
            Return.
        Done.
        If kind is "SetterDeclaration":
            Cast rename-field-text on (statement, 5, hidden).
            Return.
        Done.
        If kind is "DefineStatement" or kind is "InterfaceDefinition", cast rename-field-text on (statement, 1, hidden).
    Done.

    /// A field holding a name, renamed when the name is hidden; nothing when it holds nothing.
    Bind void to rename-field-text, given (the node statement, the number place, the map from text to text hidden):
        Define held as cast field-of on (statement, place).
        If cast is-nothing on (held), return.
        Define renamed-to as the entry for cast unquoted on (held) in hidden.
        If renamed-to is not void, cast rewrite-field on (statement, place, cast quoted on (renamed-to)).
    Done.

    // ── Books from files (`BookLoading.Expand`) ───────────────────────────

    /// The program with every book it pulls from a file brought in ahead of it — beside the file
    /// that pulls it, or in the project's `books/` — each one's own names hidden but its modules.
    Bind node or failure to with-book-files unto checker, given (the node statements):
        If one's source-file is "", return statements.
        Define folder as cast parent-of on (one's source-file).
        Define root as cast project-root on (folder).
        Define shared as "".
        If root is not "" and the path "{root}/books" is a directory, the shared becomes "{root}/books".
        Define declared-here as a map from text to fact.
        For each statement in cast every-statement-in on (statements), repeat:
            If statement's kind is "ObjectDefinition" and (cast conforms-as on (statement, "module") or cast conforms-as on (statement, "book")
                    or cast conforms-as on (statement, "region")):
                In declared-here, the entry for (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) in lowercase) becomes true.
            Done.
        Done.
        Define loaded as a map from text to text.
        Define brought as cast listed.
        Cast one's gather-books on (statements, folder, shared, declared-here, loaded, brought, a series of text) or pass the failure off.
        If the number of brought's children is 0, return statements.
        For each statement in statements's children, repeat:
            Cast brought's add on (statement).
        Done.
        Return brought.
    Done.

    /// The file a pull names, beside the puller and then in the project's books — or "".
    Bind text to book-file, given (the text book, the text folder, the text shared):
        If the path "{folder}/{book}.cufe" is a file, return "{folder}/{book}.cufe".
        If shared is not "" and the path "{shared}/{book}.cufe" is a file, return "{shared}/{book}.cufe".
        Return "".
    Done.

    /// `Gather`: each pull of a book that is a file, loaded once per file, its own pulls resolved
    /// beside IT — and a ring refused rather than followed.
    Bind void or failure to gather-books unto checker, given (the node statements, the text folder, the text shared,
            the map from text to fact declared-here, the map from text to text loaded, the node brought,
            the series of text chain):
        For each statement in cast every-statement-in on (statements), repeat:
            If statement's kind is "PullStatement":
                Define pull-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)).
                For each pulled in (cast field-of on (statement, 1))'s children, repeat:
                    Define book as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (pulled, 1)).
                    Define key as book in lowercase.
                    Define known as cast is-bundled-module on (book) or (the entry for key in declared-here) is not void.
                    If known is false:
                        For each link in chain, repeat:
                            If (link in lowercase) is key:
                                Define ring as "".
                                For each step-name in chain, repeat:
                                    The ring becomes ring joined to step-name joined to " → ".
                                Done.
                                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("the book '{book}' pulls itself, round a ring",
                                    "The ring is {ring}{book}", pull-row, "pull '{book}' from inside itself",
                                    "Break the ring — move what both of them need into a third book they can each pull.")).
                            Done.
                        Done.
                        Define found as cast book-file on (book, folder, shared).
                        If found is not "":
                            Define already as the entry for key in loaded.
                            If already is not void:
                                If cast same-path on (already, found) is false:
                                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{book}' is pulled from two different files",
                                        "One is '{cast native-path on (already)}' and the other is '{cast native-path on (found)}', and a program holds one book per NAME — what a book declares is renamed to '<name> in <book>', so two files answering to one name would collide on every declaration they have",
                                        pull-row, "pull '{book}' from both",
                                        "Rename one of them. A book's name is its namespace, so the language cannot hold two.")).
                                Done.
                            Done.
                            Otherwise:
                                In loaded, the entry for key becomes found.
                                Define file-text as "".
                                Try to:
                                    The file-text becomes read all from the file found.
                                Done.
                                In case of failure:
                                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("the book '{book}' is there but could not be read",
                                        the message of the failure, pull-row, "pull '{book}'", "Check the file's permissions.")).
                                Done.
                                Define offset as cast one's add-source on (found).
                                Define inner as cast one's loaded-tree on (found, file-text, offset) or pass the failure off.
                                Cast refuse-a-program on (inner, book, pull-row) or pass the failure off.
                                Insert book into chain.
                                Cast one's gather-books on (inner, cast parent-of on (found), shared, declared-here, loaded, brought, chain)
                                    or pass the failure off.
                                Remove item (the number of chain) from chain.
                                Cast make-private on (inner, book, a map from text to text, true).
                                For each kept in inner's children, repeat:
                                    Cast brought's add on (kept).
                                Done.
                            Done.
                        Done.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// A pulled file whose top level does something rather than declaring.
    Bind void or failure to refuse-a-program, given (the node statements, the text book, the number pull-row):
        For each statement in cast hoistable on (statements), repeat:
            Define kind as statement's kind.
            Define declares as kind is "BindStatement" or kind is "ObjectDefinition" or kind is "InterfaceDefinition"
                or kind is "GetterDeclaration" or kind is "SetterDeclaration" or kind is "UnmakerDeclaration"
                or kind is "OperatorOverloadDeclaration" or kind is "DefineStatement" or kind is "PullStatement"
                or kind is "PullRabbitStatement".
            If declares is false:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{book}' does something at its top level, so it cannot be pulled",
                    "A pulled file is a LIBRARY: its top level may DECLARE things, but anything that runs would run inside your pull, before your own first line",
                    pull-row, "pull '{book}'",
                    "Split it in two: leave the declarations in '{book}.cufe', and move the lines that DO something into a program of their own that pulls it.")).
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// Every statement, at any depth — each block's statements as well as the top level's.
    Bind series of node to every-statement-in, given (the node statements):
        Define found as a series of node.
        Cast gather-every-statement on (statements, found).
        Return found.
    Done.

    Bind void to gather-every-statement, given (the node tree, the series of node found):
        If tree's kind is "atom", return.
        If tree's kind is "list":
            For each child in tree's children, repeat:
                If child's kind is not "atom" and child's kind is not "list", insert child into found.
            Done.
        Done.
        For each child in tree's children, repeat:
            Cast gather-every-statement on (child, found).
        Done.
    Done.
Done.
